<SiteLayout path="booking-information" title="Planning & Booking Your Event | LEDJS" description="What to share when enquiring about LEDJS entertainment and how to discuss your quote, event details and booking arrangements.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><h1>From hello<br />to your event.</h1><p>The useful details to discuss before booking your entertainment.</p></div></section><article class="page-copy"><h2>Start with your date and venue.</h2><p>Tell Dave what you're celebrating, where it's happening, your approximate guest numbers and the entertainment you're interested in. For weddings, mention whether you're considering a full-evening DJ or an after-band set.</p><h2>Agree the details in your quote.</h2><p>Discuss music, playing times, equipment, access, setup and travel. Add any enhancements you want to consider. Ask for a clear written description of the final package and total cost.</p><h2>An enquiry isn't a reservation.</h2><p>Your availability, package and booking arrangements need to be confirmed directly with LEDJS. Request the applicable payment, cancellation and rescheduling terms before committing to a booking.</p><h2>Changes to your plans?</h2><p>Contact Dave directly to discuss date, venue or timing changes. Keep your enquiry reference and agreed booking information to hand.</p><a class="button" href="/contact">Talk through your event</a></article>
</SiteLayout>
